  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist1200 1451   24
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  1200 1451   25
==================================================================1200 1451   26
  Definition of Data                                              1200 1451   27
==================================================================1200 1451   28
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                1200 1451   29
==================================================================1200 1451   30
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 1200 1451   31
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       1200 1451   32
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 1200 1451   33
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              1200 1451   34
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   1200 1451   35
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     1200 1451   36
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            1200 1451   37
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  1200 1451   38
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     1200 1451   39
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     1200 1451   40
   calculates these spectra.                                      1200 1451   41
==================================================================1200 1451   42
  References                                                      1200 1451   43
==================================================================1200 1451   44
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 1200 1451   45
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   1200 1451   46
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 1200 1451   47
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 1200 1451   48
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 1200 1451   49
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    1200 1451   50
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        1200 1451   51
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    1200 1451   52
                                                                  1200 1451   53
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library1200 1451   54
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   1200 1451   55
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   1200 1451   56
  of the data, etc.                                               1200 1451   57
